---
description: Append a journal entry summarizing work done in this session
alwaysApply: true
---

# Work Journal

The user keeps a work journal at `~/Documents/Logseq/Work/pages/workjournal.md`. Append an entry at the end of each session or when the user asks.

## Entry format

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD

- Reviewed PR [[github.com/org/repo/pull/123]] — approved with minor comments
- Continued work on [[github.com/org/repo/issues/456]], added analysis in [[github.com/org/repo/issues/456/cursor]]
- Updated comment on [[github.com/org/repo/pull/789]] requesting API change
- Triaged incoming items in worktodo, moved RUN-1234 to Focus
- Worked on [[{{JIRA_ENDPOINT}}/RUN-1234]] — opened draft PR [[github.com/org/repo/pull/999]]
```

## Rules

1. **Always link.** Every mention of a GitHub issue, PR, or Jira card must be a `[[wikilink]]` using the same format as `worktodo.md` (e.g. `github.com/org/repo/pull/123`, `{{JIRA_ENDPOINT}}/KEY-123`). Link to cursor notes as `[[.../cursor]]` when relevant.
2. **Be brief.** One line per activity. State *what* happened (reviewed, commented, opened, merged, triaged, investigated) and the outcome or next step.
3. **Append, never overwrite.** If today's date heading already exists, append bullets under it. Otherwise create a new `## YYYY-MM-DD` heading at the end of the file.
4. **Create if missing.** If `workjournal.md` doesn't exist, create it with a `# Work Journal` heading before the first entry.
5. **Derive from context.** Build the entry from what you did in the session: PRs reviewed, issues investigated, code written, comments posted, todo items triaged. Don't ask the user to dictate it — infer from the conversation history.
